# round 97 (w115): is the budget what separates the two on the fold protocol? On the ten repeated splits the six gene-rule counts match the 4,131-column solve vector, but under the five-fold protocol the counts read 0.909 and the vector 0.920. The folds train each model on more genes, so a hypothesis (untested until this round) is that the richer input only pays off with more data or more steps. These arms double the budget to 400 epochs on the released split, six seeds each, counts alone and counts with the vector, against their own 200-epoch numbers 0.902 and 0.918.
